# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional common build / tool caches to keep out of the repo
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PlatformIO global artifacts (catch other firmware folders)
**/.pio/
**/.pioenvs/
**/dependencies.lock

# ESP32-C6 components/: ignore anything the IDF component manager drops here,
# but wifi_hosted is VENDORED SOURCE, not a fetched artifact. It is ESP-Hosted
# coprocessor 2.12.11 with local patches (see its CMakeLists.txt COMPONENT_
# REQUIRES block) and src/idf_component.yml depends on it by local path, not
# from the registry -- so nothing can re-fetch it. While it was ignored, the C6
# firmware could only be built on a machine that already had a copy, which is
# why no CI job could produce a C6 image. Keep it tracked.
# The trailing /* (rather than /) is required for the negation below to work:
# git will not descend into a wholly-excluded directory.
Firmware/DAQ_HAT/ESP32C6/components/*
!Firmware/DAQ_HAT/ESP32C6/components/wifi_hosted/

# Pico/CMake local build directories
**/build-*/
**/build/
# Re-include the one vendored directory the rule above would otherwise swallow:
# upstream protobuf-c's own standalone CMake recipe. It is source, not build
# output, and the vendored tree should be a faithful copy. This negation MUST
# stay after `**/build-*/` -- the last matching pattern wins.
!Firmware/DAQ_HAT/ESP32C6/components/wifi_hosted/common/protobuf-c/build-cmake/

# Python test / typecheck caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.cache/

# Node / JS artifacts
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Rust/Cargo workspace target
/target/

# Misc IDE / editor
*.code-workspace

# Mex project folder (optional internal tool) — avoid accidentally committing
.mex/
.superpowers/
